  "description": "RBE vs LET scatter: red filled circles (1 Fx oxygen) and blue filled squares (2 Fx oxygen), each with horizontal AND vertical error bars with caps and a 2nd-order fit curve of its own colour; grey circles and squares (carbon literature data) with grey bars and connecting lines overlap them; a legend box with one sample of each inside the frame (top left). Journal figure (Glowa et al. 2024, Phys Imaging Radiat Oncol 30:100581, Fig. 3 panel a): the panel (crop x 0-1440, y 0-1011 of the publisher's 3066x2182 JPEG) downscaled by 2/3 with Lanczos to 960x674 PNG so the markers are 12-14 px, a journal-page size. Closed box frame with outward major ticks every 20 keV/um and 0.2 RBE and minor ticks every 4 keV/um and 0.04 RBE (mirrored on the top and right frame lines); the corner majors (0, 180, 1.0, 2.6) have no mark of their own. Marker centres from the centroid of each marker's ink after a morphological opening that removes the 2-px bars and curves (+/- 0.5 px); the grey carbon markers are not labelled (two of them hide under the red circles at 66 and 99 keV/um, two merge at 16). Positions are image pixels, origin top-left, integer = pixel centre. Provenance and licence: fixtures/real/PROVENANCE.md.",
